    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19811" root="سعر" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُعَارٌ</span></b>  The <i>heat</i> (S, K) <i>of fire;</i> (S;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُعْرٌ</span></b> : (K:) and (tropical:)  <i>of night.</i> (A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُعْرٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also (assumed tropical:)  <i>Evil,</i> or <i>mischief:</i>
so in the saying, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَا يَنَامُ النَّاسُ مِنْ سُعَارِهِ</span> [<i>Men will
not sleep by reason of his evil,</i> or <i>mischief</i>], occurring in a trad. (TA.)

